==============================================================================
(A) RECURRENCE SIBLING: covering-min powers n^k mod Phi6(n) obey s_{k+2}=s_{k+1}-s_k
    (x^2-x+1 = Eisenstein), the SIGN-FLIP of Fibonacci s_{k+2}=s_{k+1}+s_k (x^2-x-1).
==============================================================================
  n=  4 Phi6=  13: powers(signed) [1, 4, 3, -1, -4, -3, 1]  period6=True  recurrence s_{k+2}=s_{k+1}-s_k mod Phi6: True
  n=  7 Phi6=  43: powers(signed) [1, 7, 6, -1, -7, -6, 1]  period6=True  recurrence s_{k+2}=s_{k+1}-s_k mod Phi6: True
  n= 14 Phi6= 183: powers(signed) [1, 14, 13, -1, -14, -13, 1]  period6=True  recurrence s_{k+2}=s_{k+1}-s_k mod Phi6: True
  Fibonacci: 1,1,2,3,5,8,... obeys s_{k+2}=s_{k+1}+s_k. Same shape, opposite sign.
  => the covering-min recurrence is the char.poly x^2-x+1 (roots = primitive 6th roots,
     Eisenstein Z[w], Heegner -3); Fibonacci is x^2-x-1 (roots = golden, Z[phi], sqrt5).

==============================================================================
